hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19293","Yahya ibn Said and Waki narrated to us, they said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to me from al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi, Waki said in his hadith: al-Sunabihi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Basin, and I will boast of you over the nations, so do not fight one another after me."
"19294","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid who said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim who said: I heard al-Sunabihi al-Bajali who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am your forerunner at the Basin, and boasting of you over the nations, Shubah said: Or he said: People, so do not fight one another after me."
"19295","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from Ismail from Qays from al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi the like of it."
"19296","Abbad ibn Abbad ibn Habib ibn al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah al-Muhallabi Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from Mujalid ibn Said from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Sunabihi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will boast of you over the nations, so do not return after me disbelievers striking the necks of one another."
"19297","Yunus narrated to us from Hammad ibn Zayd from al-Sunabihi, and sometimes he said: al-Sunabih."
"19298","It was recited to Sufyan while I was present: I heard Mamar narrating from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid was wounded. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking about his lodging. I said, and I was a lad: Who guides to the lodging of Khalid? He came to him wounded and sat with him."
"19299","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed us from al-Zuhri who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar informed us, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Hunayn threading through the people asking about the lodging of Khalid ibn al-Walid. A drunk was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those with him to beat him with what was in their hands. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw dust upon him."
"19300","Rawh narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threading through the people asking about the dwelling of Khalid ibn al-Walid, and he mentioned it."
"19301","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me from Ibn Ishaq, and Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Sunabihi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, and he mentioned it. Yazid ibn Harun said: al-Sunabihi is a man from Bajilah, from Ahmas."
